# Robot-Specific Standards

## URDF/Xacro

```xml
<?xml version="1.0"?>
<robot xmlns:xacro="http://ros.org/wiki/xacro" name="robot">
  <xacro:property name="wheel_radius" value="0.05"/>
  <xacro:property name="wheel_width" value="0.02"/>

  <xacro:macro name="wheel" params="prefix reflect">
    <link name="${prefix}_wheel">
      <visual><geometry><cylinder radius="${wheel_radius}" length="${wheel_width}"/></geometry></visual>
      <collision><geometry><cylinder radius="${wheel_radius}" length="${wheel_width}"/></geometry></collision>
      <inertial><mass value="0.5"/><inertia ixx="0.001" ixy="0" ixz="0" iyy="0.001" iyz="0" izz="0.001"/></inertial>
    </link>
    <joint name="${prefix}_wheel_joint" type="continuous">
      <parent link="base_link"/>
      <child link="${prefix}_wheel"/>
      <origin xyz="0 ${reflect * 0.1} 0" rpy="${-pi/2} 0 0"/>
      <axis xyz="0 0 1"/>
    </joint>
  </xacro:macro>

  <link name="base_link">
    <visual><geometry><box size="0.3 0.2 0.1"/></geometry></visual>
  </link>

  <xacro:wheel prefix="left" reflect="1"/>
  <xacro:wheel prefix="right" reflect="-1"/>
</robot>
```

## TF2 Frame Tree

```
map
 └── odom
      └── base_footprint
           └── base_link
                ├── lidar_link
                ├── camera_link
                │    └── camera_optical
                ├── imu_link
                └── left_wheel
```

## Nav2 Configuration

```yaml
bt_navigator:
  ros__parameters:
    global_frame: map
    robot_base_frame: base_link
    odom_topic: /odom

controller_server:
  ros__parameters:
    controller_frequency: 20.0
    FollowPath:
      plugin: dwb_core::DWBLocalPlanner
      max_vel_x: 0.5
      max_vel_theta: 1.0

planner_server:
  ros__parameters:
    GridBased:
      plugin: nav2_navfn_planner/NavfnPlanner
      tolerance: 0.5
      use_astar: true
```

## Sensor Integration

```python
from sensor_msgs.msg import LaserScan, Imu, Image

class SensorNode(Node):
    def __init__(self):
        super().__init__('sensor_node')
        self.lidar_pub = self.create_publisher(LaserScan, 'scan', qos_profile_sensor_data)
        self.camera_pub = self.create_publisher(Image, 'camera/image_raw', qos_profile_sensor_data)
        self.imu_pub = self.create_publisher(Imu, 'imu/data', qos_profile_sensor_data)
```

## Motor Control (Differential Drive)

```python
from geometry_msgs.msg import Twist

class MotorController(Node):
    def __init__(self):
        super().__init__('motor_controller')
        self.cmd_sub = self.create_subscription(Twist, 'cmd_vel', self.cmd_callback, 10)
        self._left_motor = Motor(pin=17)
        self._right_motor = Motor(pin=18)

    def cmd_callback(self, msg: Twist):
        linear = msg.linear.x
        angular = msg.angular.z
        left_vel = linear - angular * self.wheel_base / 2
        right_vel = linear + angular * self.wheel_base / 2
        self._left_motor.set_velocity(left_vel)
        self._right_motor.set_velocity(right_vel)
```

## Docker + DDS Gotchas

- Bridge-networked containers block the multicast DDS discovery relies on by default. Use `--network=host`, or configure an explicit peer list (CycloneDDS `<Peers>`) if containers must stay on a bridge network.
- Zero-copy DDS transport needs shared memory: size `/dev/shm` via `--shm-size` (the default 64MB is often too small for image/point-cloud topics) or transport falls back to slower loopback sockets.
